<title>CHINA: Shanghai insurance revenue up 35.2 percent.</title>
<headline>Shanghai insurance revenue up 35.2 percent.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shanghai's insurance revenue in the first 10 months of 1996 reached 4.2 billion yuan, an increase of 35.2 percent over the same 1995 period, the Shanghai Securities News said on Monday.</p>
<p>Shanghai has the most developed insurance market in China.</p>
<p>The city has six Chinese state insurance companies, one Sino-foreign joint venture insurance firm, three foreign insurance companies with licences and 40 other foreign firms with representive offices, the newspaper said.</p>
